.\" kubectl-kpm(1) - kubectl plugin shim for kpm
.TH KUBECTL-KPM 1 "2026-10-11" "kpm v0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kubectl-kpm \- kubectl plugin entrypoint for kpm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kubectl kpm
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kubectl-kpm
is the same binary as
.BR kpm (1),
installed under the
.B kubectl\-
prefix so
.B kubectl
discovers it as a plugin (
.BR "kubectl kpm \.\.\."
).
Behavior and flags match
.BR kpm (1).
.PP
Install locally with
.B make install-kubectl-plugin
(or copy the release binary named
.BR kubectl-kpm
onto
.BR PATH ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-print\-sample\-config
Print the embedded sample configuration to stdout and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print version and build metadata.
.TP
.B sample
Sample pod CPU/memory into SQLite (one-shot or daemon).
.TP
.B backup
Safe SQLite copy via
.BR VACUUM\ INTO .
.TP
.B export
Export samples as csv or tsv.
.TP
.B capacity
Live pod CPU/memory table (no SQLite).
.TP
.B recommend
Offline rightsizing from SQLite
.RB ( \-\-record ,
.BR \-\-score ).
.TP
.B tui
Interactive live heatmap
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig );
alias
.BR "capacity \-\-tui" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
make install-kubectl-plugin
kubectl kpm version
kubectl kpm sample --config ./kpm.yaml
kubectl kpm capacity --config ./kpm.yaml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Hermes Rodríguez and contributors.
